# Reuse Existing Components

Before writing any UI markup, search `$lib/components` for an existing component. Do **not** invent custom HTML when a shared primitive or domain component already covers the need.

## Checklist (before new markup)

1. Check **`packages/app/src/lib/components/ui/`** — Button, Box, Input, Dialog, Modal, Tabs, Table, Badge, Alert, Skeleton, List, Form, Avatar, Profile, Popover, Dropdown, …
2. Check domain folders — `match/`, `player/`, `lobby/`, `replay/`, `match-history/`, `widgets/`, …
3. Prefer extending via props / snippets over copying markup
4. Only write raw HTML when no existing component fits — and keep it minimal

## Prefer

```svelte
<!-- ✅ existing components -->
<script lang="ts">
	import { Button } from '$lib/components/ui/button';
	import { Badge } from '$lib/components/ui/badge';
	import { Box } from '$lib/components/ui/box';
</script>

<Box>
	<Badge>Live</Badge>
	<Button variant="primary">Join</Button>
</Box>
```

## Avoid

```svelte
<!-- ❌ hand-rolled equivalents -->
<div class="rounded border bg-card p-4">
	<span class="rounded-full bg-green-500 px-2 text-xs">Live</span>
	<button class="bg-primary px-3 py-2" onclick={...}>Join</button>
</div>
```

## Do not

- Recreate Button / Input / Dialog / Table / Badge styling with raw `<button>`, `<input>`, `<div>` + Tailwind
- Duplicate domain UI (player row, match card, lobby controls) that already lives under `$lib/components`
- Skip the search because “a quick custom div is faster”
